kunzite: Adreno 710 step 13, the first SMMU writes (kgpu=13; 1-12 unchanged).
Stream 5 (GMU) -> HLOS SMR/S2CR entry 1 -> context 1 (0 stays the GPU's, as in Linux's
adreno-smmu), only if entry 1, context 1 and stream 5 are unused. Page tables of ours in one
kernel page (3 levels, 4K granule, 39-bit VA, cache-cleaned) map a test page at the GMU's
0x60000000. Context programmed as hk's redwood SMMU took it (CBA2R VA64, CBAR stage 1, TCR2 36-bit
PA/16-bit ASID, TCR 39-bit WBWA ISH no-TTBR1, TTBR0 with ASID 1, MAIR0 Linux's, FSR cleared,
TLBIASID + TLBSYNC, SCTLR on), then S2CR/SMR; everything read back. No ATOS on this SMMU
(IDR0 ATOSNS): the GMU's own reads (steps 14-15) prove the translation. All undone at the end:
SMR, S2CR, context restored, tables freed last. Also: step 11's groups say "next:".

